<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wizlaw III, Prince of Rügen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1265–<a href="/years/1325">1325</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wizlaw III was the last Prince of Rügen of the native Slavic dynasty, ruling from 1302 to 1325 under Danish overlordship over the island and the mainland around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stralsund">Stralsund</a>. He is known as a minnesinger, whose German love songs survive in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jena">Jena</a> song <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscript</a>. He died without a son in 1325, and the principality passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomerania-wolgast">Pomerania-Wolgast</a> after a war of succession with Mecklenburg.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wizlaw-iii-prince-of-rugen.jpg" alt="Wizlaw III, Prince of Rügen" width="248" height="285" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Theodor Pyl · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wizlaw-III-RS.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
